{"key":"9421d86330da2a41","source_file":"Potts Bl - Bu.json","source_id":28436,"source_url":"concordance-breastplate-ppl-lorica","term":"Breastplate","headwords":["Breastplate"],"latin":["Lorica"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Breastplate"],"latin":["Lorica"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","AE"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"9916","subsection":null},"text":"The habergeon () = that which is strongly connected together.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"557","subsection":null},"text":"Used as synonymous with breastplate.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AE","section":"557","subsection":"3"},"text":"The brigandine () = the force and strength of fighting and resisting. The reason a brigandine has this signification, is that it girds the breast, and all the strength of fighting and resisting is from the breast through the arms.","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"breastplate-9421d8","url":"/meta/potts/breastplate-9421d8/"}